      "cr": 1,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Valorian Stormweave.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. XP ledger: level 2, power rating 4 → CR 1 as a spellcaster. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Dead Man Who Took His Secrets With Him</strong> — Mages' Guild (Senior Enforcer)</p><p>Status: Deceased — killed by Archie Miser in a public market, 1040 BF. Ruled 'justifiable magical defense' by Onyx Hand tribunal.</p><p>Valorian Stormweave was a Senior Enforcer of the Mages' Guild who—according to Lady Bloomia's testimony—was present at the Royal Vault on the morning of Princess Peach's assassination in 955 BF. He allegedly delayed the Solstice Crown delivery, knew Bloomia's name without introduction, smiled 'like a predator who has confirmed the location of its prey,' and was part of the Guild's involvement in 'the arrangement.' He lived for eighty-five years after allegedly helping murder a princess. Then Archie Miser killed him in a public market during an altercation that an Onyx Hand tribunal ruled justifiable. The only person who could have testified about Guild complicity in the assassination is now ash. Whether this is cosmic justice, cosmic irony, or cosmic convenience depends entirely on who you ask—and EVERYONE has an opinion. Waluigi has spent considerable time examining this death because it sits at the intersection of two stories that should have nothing to do with each other: Archie's chaotic journey and the eighty-five-year-old assassination conspiracy. The intersection is either coincidence or something much worse. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Staff</strong> — “The Dead Man Who Took His Secrets With Him”</li><li><strong>Fire Magic</strong> — “Archie—the walking disaster, the entropy-bleeder, the man who resolves everything with fireballs—accidentally destroyed the most important piece of evidence in an eighty-five-year-old murder investigation.”</li><li><strong>Keen Records</strong> — “Bloomia describes encountering two figures in dark robes embroidered with silver staves—Mages' Guild identification—arguing with the vault master Cornelius about 'unauthorized magical access' to the Solstice Crown's”</li><li><strong>Guild Spellcasting</strong> — “Mages' Guild (Senior Enforcer)”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/valorian_stormweave</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/valorian_stormweave</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
